{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And a woman, if she has a discharge.</b> As it is said: ״בעצלתים ימך המקרה״ — because a woman who is negligent in examining herself for her blood renders impure, retroactively, all purities she had performed, and becomes smitten and impoverished, as we find with the maidservant of Rabbi Gamliel, who would move barrels from place to place and would examine herself between each and every one. In the end she examined herself and found herself impure, and had she not examined herself between each and every one, they would all have been impure. Therefore the Sages said: every hand that examines frequently in women is praiseworthy."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {0 "The verse cited, בעצלתים ימך המקרה, is from Proverbs 10:26, here applied midrashically to the consequences of a woman's neglect of self-examination."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:13.915790174Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}